IMPORT prelude

-- Federal Proceedings (Costs) Act 1981 (Cth) — THE NOUNS, THE RULES AND THE
-- TOP-LEVEL GOAL. Source: ../registers/source-bundle/C2004A02401.txt
-- (compilation No. 15, 10 June 2025). The litigant asks: "Can the court give
-- me a costs certificate; what is the most the Attorney-General can pay me;
-- can my certificate be vacated; can I be paid now?"

§ `Nouns`

-- ss 6-10A: the route to a costs certificate.
DECLARE `Route` IS ONE OF
    `respondent to a Federal appeal that succeeded on a question of law or on damages`
    `appellant whose respondent cannot pay, would suffer undue hardship, or cannot be found`
    `appellant with no respondent, the appeal succeeding on a question of law`
    `party to a civil cause given a new trial on a question of law`
    `accused given a new trial on appeal against conviction on a question of law`
    `appellant in a family law appeal succeeding on law, each party bearing their own costs`
    `party to proceedings made abortive, or discontinued through no party's fault`
    `party, other than the decision-maker, to a Tribunal review that must be reheard`
    `none`

-- s 14(1).
DECLARE `Who I am` IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a company with paid-up capital under $200,000, not related to a larger one`
    `the Commonwealth, a State, the NT, their authority, or suing for them`
    `a company with paid-up capital of $200,000 or more, or related to one`

-- Schedule.
DECLARE `Forum` IS ONE OF
    `the High Court`
    `the Federal Court`
    `the Federal Circuit and Family Court`
    `a Territory Supreme Court`
    `another Territory court`
    `the Administrative Review Tribunal`

DECLARE `Costs case` HAS
    `my route`                                              IS A `Route`
    `who I am`                                              IS A `Who I am`
    `the forum`                                             IS A `Forum`
    `my costs`                                              IS A NUMBER
    `the prescribed amount, if higher`                      IS A NUMBER
    -- s 15
    `the other side appealed further and succeeded`         IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 17
    `the other side has appealed or sought leave`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `notice of no intended appeal was given`                IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Costs position` HAS
    `the court may grant me a certificate`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the most the Attorney-General may pay`                 IS A NUMBER
    `my certificate is vacated under s 15`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Attorney-General may pay now under s 17`           IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Rules`

-- s 14(1)(a)-(g).
@ref s 14
GIVEN c IS A `Costs case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I am excluded` c IF
        c's `who I am` EQUALS `the Commonwealth, a State, the NT, their authority, or suing for them`
    OR  c's `who I am` EQUALS `a company with paid-up capital of $200,000 or more, or related to one`

@ref ss 6-10A, 14
GIVEN c IS A `Costs case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a certificate may be granted` c IF
        NOT (c's `my route` EQUALS `none`)
    AND NOT (`I am excluded` c)

-- s 15: certificates under ss 6, 7 and 9 are vacated if the other side
-- appeals and succeeds.
@ref s 15
GIVEN c IS A `Costs case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the certificate can be vacated` c IF
        c's `my route` EQUALS `respondent to a Federal appeal that succeeded on a question of law or on damages`
    OR  c's `my route` EQUALS `appellant whose respondent cannot pay, would suffer undue hardship, or cannot be found`
    OR  c's `my route` EQUALS `appellant in a family law appeal succeeding on law, each party bearing their own costs`

@ref s 15
GIVEN c IS A `Costs case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `my certificate is vacated` c IF
        `a certificate may be granted` c
    AND `the certificate can be vacated` c
    AND c's `the other side appealed further and succeeded`

-- Schedule; s 18(1): the amount, or a higher prescribed amount.
@ref s 18(1), Schedule
GIVEN c IS A `Costs case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the cap for` c MEANS
    IF c's `the prescribed amount, if higher` GREATER THAN scheduled THEN c's `the prescribed amount, if higher` ELSE scheduled
    WHERE
        scheduled MEANS
            CONSIDER c's `the forum`
            WHEN `the High Court` THEN 5000
            WHEN `the Federal Court` THEN 3000
            WHEN `the Federal Circuit and Family Court` THEN 2000
            WHEN `a Territory Supreme Court` THEN 3000
            WHEN `another Territory court` THEN 1000
            WHEN `the Administrative Review Tribunal` THEN 2000

-- s 16(2): no more than the costs; s 18(2)-(2A): no more than the cap, except
-- for s 10 certificates.
@ref ss 16(2), 18(2)-(2A)
GIVEN c IS A `Costs case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most payable for` c MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`a certificate may be granted` c)) OR `my certificate is vacated` c THEN 0
        IF c's `my route` EQUALS `party to proceedings made abortive, or discontinued through no party's fault`
            THEN c's `my costs`
        IF c's `my costs` AT MOST `the cap for` c THEN c's `my costs`
        OTHERWISE `the cap for` c

-- s 17(1)-(2): for a certificate that can be vacated, only if satisfied it
-- will not be, or entitled to presume so (no appeal and a notice given).
@ref s 17
GIVEN c IS A `Costs case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Attorney-General may pay now` c IF
        `the most payable for` c GREATER THAN 0
    AND (   NOT (`the certificate can be vacated` c)
         OR (    NOT (c's `the other side has appealed or sought leave`)
             AND c's `notice of no intended appeal was given`))

@ref ss 6-18, Schedule
@export default The position of a litigant under the Federal Proceedings (Costs) Act 1981 (Cth): whether the court may grant them a costs certificate (a respondent to a Federal appeal that succeeded on law or on damages, an appellant whose respondent cannot pay, an appellant with no respondent, a party or accused given a new trial on a point of law, a family law appellant, a party to abortive or discontinued proceedings, or a party to a Tribunal review that must be reheard; not governments, their authorities, or companies with $200,000 paid-up capital: ss 6-10A, 14); the most the Attorney-General may pay (the costs, capped by the Schedule for the court, except for abortive proceedings: ss 16, 18); whether the certificate is vacated by the other side's later success (s 15); and whether the Attorney-General may pay now (s 17). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Costs case`  @desc My route to a certificate, who I am, the court, my costs, and any further appeal or notice
GIVETH A `Costs position`
`the costs position for` c MEANS
    `Costs position` OF `a certificate may be granted` c, `the most payable for` c, `my certificate is vacated` c, `the Attorney-General may pay now` c
